  <title>2.12.3: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00589</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.12.3: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>8ba1e9b0-5e17-4815-8e36-85fe05da0f2c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>An artist is designing a sculpture to be displayed hanging in the lobby of a museum. She is using \(x\) wooden rods and \(y\) metal pipes.</para>
<list>
  <item>Each wooden rod, \(x\), weighs 4 pounds.</item>
  <item>Each metal pipe, \(y\), weighs 7 pounds. </item>
  <item>The total weight of these materials cannot be more than 510 pounds. </item>
</list>
<para>Which of these ordered pairs represents an amount of materials that meets the artist’s constraints?</para>
 </section>
</content>
</document>
